  message: "Done. Merged 173e539114 (PR #346). edge.meta.channel de-overloaded to a single referent — the dataflow conduit/topic. The 3 non-conduit edge emit sites are fixed: (1) websocket.py references edge — dropped channel=ep.event (endpoint id is the edge dst; not relocated to url_path since ep.event is a route path for path-based WS but a consumer class for Django Channels, not reliably a URL); (2) websocket.py calls edge — dropped redundant channel=path_str (route already on meta.url_path); (3) annotation_convention.py dispatches_to edge — dropped redundant channel=target_name (target is the edge dst). Remaining channel= edge sites (event_publishes in ipc/tauri/message_queue/message_dispatch/event_sourcing/annotation:270/websocket:840/dataflow + crypto_flow/yjs_crdt conduits) are all the dataflow-conduit referent. channel + url_path now registered in axis_meta_keys MetaKeySpec with the conduit-vs-route contract. No Edge.create signature change. Behavioral repro on merged code: a @hg:dispatches annotation now yields a dispatches_to edge with dst='typescript:src/handler.ts:1-1:handle_join:function' and NO 'channel' in meta (meta keys = ['mechanism']) — was meta.channel='handle_join'. Production-path test: test_annotation_convention_linker.py (the dispatches_to assertion flips to the canonical dst + asserts 'channel' not in meta); test_websocket.py green with channel removed from the references/calls bridge edges (event_publishes topic channel at :594 unchanged). Scope note: Symbol.meta.channel on the synthetic annotated-dispatcher node (annotation_convention:350) is a SYMBOL not an edge — out of this edge-meta finding's scope, left as-is."  # 67a7
